From: Jordi Kroon <jkroon@onyourmarks.agency>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:16:00 +0200
Subject: ext/standard: Fix 1-char relative Location redirects after GH-23467

8196275133e changed the relative-Location check from location_len > 1 to
> 0, so a single-character Location began resolving against the request
path instead of the host root as before.

Closes GH-23521

(cherry picked from commit 64664758cd8ee5928acf25b3f9ae11c7571c1b39)
(cherry picked from commit b9e45bc1e68671514e174c07664db0d5f15f2ac4)
(cherry picked from commit efd5b568672b680b155c8b4500a8abea2da984c9)
---
 ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c                  |  2 +-
 .../tests/http/http_empty_location_redirect.phpt   |  2 +-
 .../http/http_single_char_location_redirect.phpt   | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 ext/standard/tests/http/http_single_char_location_redirect.phpt

diff --git a/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c b/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c
index f09ad2a..4a36874 100644
--- a/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c
+++ b/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c
@@ -1091,7 +1091,7 @@ finish:
 			{
 				char *loc_path = NULL;
 				if (*header_info.location != '/') {
-					if (header_info.location_len > 0 && resource->path) {
+					if (header_info.location_len > 1 && resource->path) {
 						char *s = strrchr(ZSTR_VAL(resource->path), '/');
 						if (!s) {
 							s = ZSTR_VAL(resource->path);
diff --git a/ext/standard/tests/http/http_empty_location_redirect.phpt b/ext/standard/tests/http/http_empty_location_redirect.phpt
index a7f99bf..399c8c6 100644
